# v12.0-audited migration: source files deleted or renamed on this branch
# that were already applied to $HOME from before it. `chezmoi apply` never
# removes a target just because its source disappeared -- that is what this
# file is for. Caught by `chezmoi diff` showing these as neither modified
# nor removed (nothing to diff, since they are no longer managed at all)
# while `ls ~/.config/...` proved they were still sitting there.
#
# The nvim ones matter most: lazy.nvim's `{ import = "plugins" }` loads
# every *.lua file in that directory with no allowlist, unlike the zsh
# modules' explicit `_mods` array -- a stale plugins/avante.lua or
# structurizr.lua left on disk would still load and define plugins/keymaps
# this repo no longer configures.
.config/nvim/lua/plugins/avante.lua
.config/nvim/lua/plugins/structurizr.lua
.config/nvim/KEYBINDINGS.md
.config/zsh/c4.zsh
.config/chawan/config.toml
.local/bin/arc-open
# The c4-architect skill directory was renamed to d2-architect (git mv), but
# chezmoi has no rename tracking -- caught the same way as the six above:
# ~/.claude/skills/c4-architect/SKILL.md was still on disk with its old
# Structurizr-DSL instructions, still answering to /c4-architect.
.claude/skills/c4-architect/SKILL.md
.claude/skills/c4-architect

# tmux dropped from the baseline once the zellij project layouts covered
# everything it did (see .chezmoitemplates/Brewfile and dot_config/zellij/).
# tpm's own plugin clones under .config/tmux/plugins/ are left alone --
# still guarded in .chezmoiignore.tmpl, and `rm -rf ~/.config/tmux` after
# apply is the one manual step this file cannot do for you (chezmoiremove
# targets have to be listed explicitly, not globbed).
.config/tmux/tmux.conf
.config/tmux/layouts/layout.sh
.config/tmux/layouts/pick.sh
